.Dd July 18, 2026
.Dt MOUNT_TARFS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount_tarfs
.Nd mount a tar archive as a read-only file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Ar tarfile
.Ar mount_point
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility attaches a
.Xr tarfs 5
file system to the global file system name space.
The archive
.Ar tarfile
must be a regular file containing an uncompressed POSIX ustar
.Pq optional PAX
stream.
.Pp
.Nm
always mounts read-only.
If the
.Nm tarfs
file system type is not already present, the utility attempts to load
it with
.Xr vfsload 3 .
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl o Ar options
Options are specified with a
.Fl o
flag followed by a comma-separated string of options.
See
.Xr mount 8
for standard options.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mount_tarfs /var/db/images/tree.tar /mnt
.Ed
.Pp
Decompress zstd first (kernel has no zstd):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zstd -d archive.tar.zst -o /tmp/archive.tar
mount_tarfs /tmp/archive.tar /mnt
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tar 1 ,
.Xr tarfs 5 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr umount 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
appeared in the
.Dx
tarfs port.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
